* Parts for the opamp circuit.

* 1N4148 small-signal diode (common model)
.model D1N4148 D(IS=2.52n RS=0.568 N=1.752 CJO=4p M=0.4 TT=20n BV=100 IBV=100u)

* Generic opamp in the NE5532/OPA2134 class, powered from +/-15 V.
* - DC gain 100 dB, GBW approx. 10 MHz (single pole)
* - output swing limited to approx. +/-13.5 V (soft limiting with tanh)
* - input noise approx. 5 nV/rtHz via an equivalent noise resistor of 1.5k
*   (ngspice computes no noise for behavioural sources, but does for a resistor)
* Pins: non-inverting, inverting, output
.subckt OPAMP inp inn out
RN inp inp2 1.5k
RIN inp2 inn 10Meg
* transconductance -> integrator: A0 = gm*R1 = 1e5, pole at 100 Hz -> GBW 10 MHz
G1 0 n1 inp2 inn 1m
R1 n1 0 100Meg
C1 n1 0 15.9p
* clamp diodes: keep the integrator from running away when saturated (windup)
VCP cp 0 DC 14
VCN cn 0 DC -14
DCP n1 cp DCLAMP
DCN cn n1 DCLAMP
.model DCLAMP D(IS=1e-14 N=1)
* output limiting and low output impedance
BO o1 0 V={ 13.5*tanh(V(n1)/13.5) }
RO o1 out 10
.ends OPAMP
